  (text "[0] MODE Register - Cycle control and status\n============================================\nREAD    WRITE\n----- ---------\nx x B 0 b 0 0 0  - RUN\nx x B 0 x 0 0 1  - STOP\nx x B 1 x 0 0 1  - Run one instruction cycle\nx x B 1 x 0 1 1  - Run one debug operation\nx x B x x 1 x x  - RESET\n              |--- DEBUG_STOP (stop the PC)\n            |----- DEBUG_MODE (0 = instruction, 1 = debug)\n          |------- DEBUG_RESET (global reset)\n        |--------- BREAKPOINT ACTIVE\n      |----------- DEBUG_REQX (trigger a debug cycle)\n\n    |------------- AT_BKP\n"
    (at 57.15 -19.05 0)
    (effects (font (face "Consolas") (size 1 1)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 326149df-fa24-40d2-98b0-28a05675535b)
  )
  (text "[1] OP Register - Debug Operations\n================================================================\n0000000 x  - WRBKP (address of breakpoint)\n0000001 i  - MEMRD (address in ADDR, set i for post increment)\n0000010 i  - MEMWR (address in ADDR, set i for post increment)\n0000011 i  - REGRD (address in ADDR)\n0000100 i  - REGWR (address in ADDR)\n0000101 i  - CCRD  (address in ADDR selects CCREGX)\n0000110 i  - PCRD  (address in ADDR selectd PCNEXTX)\n0000111 x  - INSTRD read the current instruction\n        |\n        |---- DEBUG_INC\n-------\n   |--------- DEBUG_OP\n\nAddress increments happen on access to the data high-byte\nat the end of a read or write cycle"
    (at 105.41 -35.56 0)
    (effects (font (face "Consolas") (size 1 1)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 50c221be-c87e-4d6b-8435-9f99c5c79181)
  )
  (text "Debug Registers\n=================================\n0 MODE - RUN / STOP / ISTEP / DSTEP\n1 OP   - Debug instruction\n2 AL   - Address Low Byte\n3 AH   - Address High Byte\n4 DL   - Data Low Byte and DEBUG_ARGX\n5 DH   - Data High Byte\n6 ARGL - Argument Low Byte\n7 ARGH - Argument High Byte\n"
    (at 57.15 -49.53 0)
    (effects (font (face "Consolas") (size 1 1)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid e5e708eb-42bb-4614-b9d1-16ee85c5eea6)
  )
  (text "If INCX is set, then trigger a request\n - on every high byte read or write to memory, reg, pc\n - on every low byte of CC\n\nDEBUG_ADDR_OUT = {DEBUG_ADDR[15:1],0} for memory cycles (inc by 2)\nDEBUG_ADDR_OUT = DEBUG_ADDR[15:0]  for non-memory cycles (inc by 1)"
    (at 57.15 -3.81 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid ff4307c8-1512-4c79-8a3e-1ea5e07da61e)
  )

